From eae5e385b5271c566eb56948e43fe19020c09473 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:05:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm: add optional NUMA-local i_mmap sharding

hulk inclusion
category: feature
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/9771

--------------------------------

Concurrent mmap and munmap operations on the same regular file serialize
on a single address_space i_mmap_rwsem. Split contended reverse-mapping
trees into four cacheline-aligned shards per NUMA domain, supporting up
to eight domains and allocating each domain's state on its NUMA node.

Select a stable home node and shard index for each mm and inherit both
across fork. Convert eligible mappings under the central write lock and
publish the populated shard set with release ordering. Track VMA counts
independently of tree layout so mapping_mapped() remains valid during
conversion. Store the new mapping and mm state in existing KABI reserves.

Route VMA updates through the selected shard and make file rmap, unmap,
memory-failure, khugepaged, pagewalk and uprobe traversal cover every
shard. Preserve locked-rmap and mm_take_all_locks() semantics by acquiring
all relevant shard locks in a fixed order, including all-or-nothing
trylock handling.

Insert each forked file VMA immediately after its parent under the
appropriate tree lock, updating the VMA count before copying page tables.
Retain the existing unlink batches keyed by struct file, with shard-aware
locking for each batch.

Gate the capability with CONFIG_I_MMAP_SHARDS and a default-false static
key controlled by the boot-only i_mmap_opt=<bool> parameter. Enable dynamic
sharding only with i_mmap_opt=on after sufficient lock contention. Exclude
shmem, DAX and hugetlb mappings from conversion, and retain the central
tree when sharding is disabled or allocation fails.

Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
